  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q47-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Given $0<\\theta<\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac13$, find the exact value of $\\sin^2\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3-2\\sqrt2}{6}$",
      "worked": "Since $\\theta$ is in the first quadrant, $\\cos\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac13\\right)^2}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $\\cos\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{2}\\\\\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\frac{1-\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}}{2}\\\\\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\frac{3-2\\sqrt2}{6}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
